Fabrikam Insurance indexes scanned claim forms (JPEG files) from Blob Storage. The skillset runs an OCR skill with <code>context</code> <code>/document/normalized_images/*</code>, but the OCR text field stays empty and no errors are reported. The indexer configuration is:
<pre>"parameters": { "configuration": {
  "dataToExtract": "contentAndMetadata",
  "parsingMode": "default"
} }</pre>
Which setting fixes the problem?

Woodgrove Bank's prompt agent uses an MCP tool declared with <code>require_approval="always"</code>. The app collects the reviewer's decision as shown:
<pre>ref = {"agent_reference": {"name": agent.name, "type": "agent_reference"}}
response = openai.responses.create(input="Open an issue for the failed deployment", extra_body=ref)

input_list = []
for item in response.output:
    if item.type == "mcp_approval_request":
        input_list.append(McpApprovalResponse(
            type="mcp_approval_response",
            approve=True,
            approval_request_id=item.id,
        ))

response = openai.responses.create(input=input_list, extra_body=ref)</pre>
Which argument must the second <code>responses.create</code> call include so that the approval is applied to the pending tool call?

Adventure Works evaluates its support agent with the criterion below. One dataset row returns a Violence <code>score</code> of 5 and the default threshold applies.
<pre>{
    "type": "azure_ai_evaluator",
    "name": "Violence",
    "evaluator_name": "builtin.violence",
    "data_mapping": {"query": "{{item.query}}", "response": "{{item.response}}"}
}</pre>
Which <b>TWO</b> statements are correct?

